The popup decision (frontend) and the actual approval decision (backend) are computed independently — the frontend checks locally-loaded function-code flags, the backend re-checks the same thing against the database at save time — and these two calculations aren't guaranteed to agree for the per-function-code case. The toggle-based scenarios were fixed by exposing the toggle value directly to the frontend; the per-function-code case needs the same treatment, or a shared source of truth between the two.
